*Dedicated to Daniel Hall*

We fled the sea, a burning sight tonight;
I hold your ghost in fading light tonight.

They ask for proof of towns reduced to smoke;
I stand in rain, my knuckles white tonight.

Your hand slipped from my grip beneath the wave;
The deep ocean swallowed all your laughter bright tonight.

In camps of mud and plastic, winter howls;
No foreign soil will make me right tonight.

I carry heavy stones within my chest;
I wrap my arms in dark and hold them tight tonight.

For Daniel Hall, record the exile’s grief—
Belovèd, take my sorrow in your sight tonight.
